WEBVTT

00:00.050 --> 00:02.220
This is the NbS Tool.

00:02.390 --> 00:04.560
Every analysis follows the same eight

00:04.560 --> 00:07.120
phases, from a first look at the map to a

00:07.120 --> 00:08.770
document for a funder.

00:08.770 --> 00:10.960
Here is the whole workflow.

00:10.960 --> 00:13.040
Phase zero is optional.

00:13.040 --> 00:14.260
Explore the map.

00:14.260 --> 00:16.730
Switch layers on from the rail on the

00:16.730 --> 00:17.320
left.

00:17.320 --> 00:20.160
Read the legend at the bottom right and

00:20.160 --> 00:22.100
search for a place by name.

00:22.100 --> 00:23.090
Phase one.

00:23.090 --> 00:25.510
Select your area of interest.

00:25.520 --> 00:28.370
Draw a polygon on the map or upload a

00:28.370 --> 00:29.420
boundary file.

00:29.450 --> 00:31.310
The tool measures the area.

00:31.380 --> 00:33.920
Check the hectares, then continue.

00:33.920 --> 00:36.740
Phase two is site characterisation.

00:36.830 --> 00:38.800
What is in your area today?

00:38.800 --> 00:40.450
Four tabs describe it.

00:40.800 --> 00:43.870
General, nature, people and climate.

00:43.870 --> 00:46.170
The information button on each card shows

00:46.170 --> 00:47.750
where a number comes from.

00:47.850 --> 00:50.770
Phase three is the threat profile.

00:50.770 --> 00:53.200
What is happening to the site and where it

00:53.280 --> 00:55.300
is heading if nothing changes?

00:55.420 --> 00:57.790
It shows past disturbance, current

00:57.790 --> 00:59.890
pressure and a business as usual

00:59.890 --> 01:00.910
projection.

01:00.910 --> 01:02.960
Phase four is the decision.

01:03.010 --> 01:06.200
For each ecosystem, switch on a pathway.

01:06.200 --> 01:08.570
Protect, manage or restore.

01:08.570 --> 01:10.860
Tick the activities your project will

01:10.880 --> 01:11.710
carry out.

01:11.710 --> 01:14.020
Then set the duration and the carbon

01:14.020 --> 01:14.710
option.

01:14.710 --> 01:17.220
Phase five shows the potential benefits

01:17.230 --> 01:19.430
for nature, people and climate.

01:19.430 --> 01:21.690
These are screening estimates, not

01:21.710 --> 01:22.820
measurements.

01:22.930 --> 01:25.270
Finish the analysis to save it to My

01:25.270 --> 01:25.710
Project.

01:25.710 --> 01:27.680
Saving needs a free account.

01:27.680 --> 01:30.920
Phase six is monitoring planning.

01:30.930 --> 01:33.380
The activities you chose carry over.

01:33.380 --> 01:36.320
The tool proposes indicators, methods and

01:36.320 --> 01:37.470
frequencies.

01:37.470 --> 01:40.250
Review them, then generate the plan.

01:40.250 --> 01:42.770
Phase seven, generate documents.

01:43.010 --> 01:45.860
Choose the Feasibility Document or the CCB

01:45.860 --> 01:47.520
Standards template.

01:47.520 --> 01:49.650
Fields from your analysis are already

01:49.750 --> 01:50.510
filled in.

01:50.510 --> 01:52.920
Complete the rest, then download an

01:52.920 --> 01:54.480
editable Word file.

01:54.480 --> 01:57.150
After the analysis, manage your work in My

01:57.230 --> 01:58.040
Project.

01:58.070 --> 02:00.850
Find, filter and search every project.

02:01.200 --> 02:03.780
Open one to see its overview, its

02:03.780 --> 02:06.900
analysis, its monitoring plan and its MRV

02:06.900 --> 02:07.510
data.

02:07.510 --> 02:10.880
The tool gives you a baseline and a plan.

02:10.930 --> 02:13.600
Always verify the results in the field.

02:13.600 --> 02:16.050
To begin, open the Interactive Map.
